   "narration": {
    "en": "Major Somnath Sharma was the first recipient of the Param Vir Chakra, India's highest gallantry award. The events began in August 1947 when Pakistan launched Operation Gulmarg to take Kashmir, breaking its commitment to Maharaja Hari Singh."
